      "updated": 1745108074406,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Builder pattern to get rid of a “telescoping constructor”.\n-  Use the Builder pattern when you want your code to be able to \ncreate different representations of some product. Ex: stone and wooden houses.\n- Use the Builder to construct Composite trees or other complex objects.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Builder pattern to get rid of a “telescoping constructor”.\n-  Use the Builder pattern when you want your code to be able to \ncreate different representations of some product. Ex: stone and wooden houses.\n- Use the Builder to construct Composite trees or other complex objects.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
