      "updated": 1745211894397,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Singleton pattern when a class in your program should have just a \nsingle instance available to all clients; for example, a single database \nobject shared by different parts of the program.\n- Use the Singleton pattern when you need stricter control over global \nvariables.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Singleton pattern when a class in your program should have just a \nsingle instance available to all clients; for example, a single database \nobject shared by different parts of the program.\n- Use the Singleton pattern when you need stricter control over global \nvariables.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
