      "updated": 1745211885595,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Prototype pattern when your code shouldn’t depend on the concrete \nclasses of objects that you need to copy.\n- Use the pattern when you want to reduce the number of subclasses that only \ndiffer in the way they initialize their respective objects.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
