      "updated": 1745211906491,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Adapter class when you want to use some existing class, but its \ninterface isn’t compatible with the rest of your code.\n\n- Use the pattern when you want to reuse several existing subclasses that \nlack some common functionality that can’t be added to the superclass.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Adapter class when you want to use some existing class, but its \ninterface isn’t compatible with the rest of your code.\n\n- Use the pattern when you want to reuse several existing subclasses that \nlack some common functionality that can’t be added to the superclass.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
