      "versionNonce": 1715523177,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1744760520774,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n-  Use the Decorator pattern when you need to be able to assign extra behaviors to \nobjects at runtime without breaking the code that uses these objects.\n\n-  Use the pattern when it’s awkward or not possible to extend an object’s behavior \nusing inheritance.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n-  Use the Decorator pattern when you need to be able to assign extra behaviors to \nobjects at runtime without breaking the code that uses these objects.\n\n-  Use the pattern when it’s awkward or not possible to extend an object’s behavior \nusing inheritance.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
