      "text": "When we Work with a broad set of objects that belong to\na sophisticated library or framework, you’d need to\ninitialize all of those objects, keep track of dependencies,\nexecute methods in the correct order, and so on.\n\nBusiness logic of your classes would become tightly coupled\nto the implementation details of 3rd-party classes, making\nit hard to comprehend and maintain.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When we Work with a broad set of objects that belong to a sophisticated library or framework, you’d need to initialize all of those objects, keep track of dependencies, execute methods in the correct order, and so on.\n\nBusiness logic of your classes would become tightly coupled to the implementation details of 3rd-party classes, making it hard to comprehend and maintain.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
