      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1745216579646,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Iterator pattern when your collection has a complex data structure under the\nhood, but you want to hide its complexity from clients (either for convenience or\nsecurity reasons).\n- Use the pattern to reduce duplication of the traversal code across your app.\n- Use the Iterator when you want your code to be able to traverse different data\nstructures or when types of these structures are unknown beforehand.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Iterator pattern when your collection has a complex data structure under the hood, but you want to hide its complexity from clients (either for convenience or security reasons).\n- Use the pattern to reduce duplication of the traversal code across your app.\n- Use the Iterator when you want your code to be able to traverse different data structures or when types of these structures are unknown beforehand.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
