      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7AV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1614029091,
      "version": 5163,
      "versionNonce": 2116456515,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1745281188856,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Mediator pattern when it’s hard to change some of the classes because they are\ntightly coupled to a bunch of other classes.\n- Use the pattern when you can’t reuse a component in a different program because it’s\ntoo dependent on other components.\n- Use the Mediator when you find yourself creating tons of component subclasses just to\nreuse some basic behavior in various contexts.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Mediator pattern when it’s hard to change some of the classes because they are tightly coupled to a bunch of other classes.\n- Use the pattern when you can’t reuse a component in a different program because it’s too dependent on other components.\n- Use the Mediator when you find yourself creating tons of component subclasses just to reuse some basic behavior in various contexts.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
