      "updated": 1745453297410,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Memento pattern when you want to produce snapshots of the object’s state to be\nable to restore a previous state of the object.\n- Use the pattern when direct access to the object’s fields/getters/setters violates its\nencapsulation.",
      "fontSize": 29.79547481958467,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Applicability\n\n- Use the Memento pattern when you want to produce snapshots of the object’s state to be able to restore a previous state of the object.\n- Use the pattern when direct access to the object’s fields/getters/setters violates its encapsulation.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
